  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0 — hardening in lockstep with the family: a locally-operating CryptographyClient's CryptographicException now maps to the same fail-closed PqDecryptionException as the remote path (one message, no oracle), and the engine now rejects any provider-returned content key that is not exactly 32 bytes. No change to the provider's API or the .pqfe v2 container format, which remains FROZEN for the 1.x line. See CHANGELOG.md.",
